# Test: Invalid icm:about usage with literal value
# This test validates that icm:about must be an IRI, not a literal
# Should FAIL with: "icm:about must be an IRI (resource reference), not a literal"

@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/> .
@prefix icm:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentCommonModel/> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

################################################################################
# VIOLATION: icm:about with literal value
#
# Common mistake: Using a literal string instead of an IRI reference
# The icm:about property MUST reference another resource (Intent, Expectation, etc.)
################################################################################

# WRONG - using literal string
ex:IR1
  a icm:IntentReport ;
  icm:about "my-intent-name" ;  # WRONG: This is a literal, not an IRI
  icm:result true
  .
